Z||000000||vinnywolfe||04-12-2000||11:50 PM||||i recently purchased a set of cragar 5 star rims with bf goodrich tires.  i purchased them used so i can't really return them.<BR>the rims are 15" with two sets of mounting holes, so i assumed that they were universal and would fit. they didn't. i took both front rotors off (bearings and all) and i was wondering if anyone knows if there are any stock gm rotor/hubs that would fit(same inner and outer bearing size) and have the larger bolt pattern that i need to use the cragars.  i know i'll probably have to change the calipers also, but i was planing on doing a brake upgrade anyway (90-95 grand am/cavalier).  i would appreciate any information anyone has.  it would eliminate a lot of trial and error.<P>thanks,<P>vince wolfenbarger<P>wolfenbargers@provide.net<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||04-13-2000||02:08 AM||||If you can figure this one out, you'll be a Fiero hero. The Grand Am/Cavalier rotors, even the early to mid 90's cars are still the same bolt pattern as the Fiero, 5 bolts with 100mm spacing. I've not heard of anyone doing that swap yet anyway. My guess is that those wheels are not for the newer metric wheels.||||reg||1
